{"tool_name":"selsim","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"selsim","home":"https://popmodels.cancercontrol.cancer.gov/gsr/packages/selsim","license":"Not licensed","summary":"A program for Monte Carlo simulation of DNA polymorphism data for a recombining region within which a single bi-allelic site has experienced natural selection.","addition_date":"2017-08-20T15:58:56Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:02:12.532420Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"collections":["Animal and Crop Genomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:selsim","credit":[{"email":"gmcoop@ucdavis.edu","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"spencer@well.ox.ac.uk","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/trvrb/selsim"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["animalandcropgenomics"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Modelling and simulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2426"}]}],"name":"SelSim","owner":"admin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bth417","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: SelSim is a program for Monte Carlo simulation of DNA polymorphism data for a recombining region within which a single bi-allelic site has experienced natural selection. SelSim allows simulation from either a fully stochastic model of, or deterministic approximations to, natural selection within a coalescent framework. A number of different mutation models are available for simulating surrounding neutral variation. The package enables a detailed exploration of the effects of different models and strengths of selection on patterns of diversity. This provides a tool for the statistical analysis of both empirical data and methods designed to detect natural selection. \u00a9 Oxford University Press 2004; all rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Coop G."},{"name":"Spencer C.C.A."}],"citationCount":96,"date":"2004-12-12T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioi